= Larynx
{parent=Anatomy}

= Phonation
{parent=Larynx}
{wiki}

Production of voiced <sound waves> through oscillation of the <vocal folds>, driven by air from the <lungs>. Resonances of the vocal tract then modify that source.<Taking Care of Your Voice by the National Institute on Deafness and Other Communication Disorders>[What is voice?]{ref}

= Laryngeal muscle
{parent=Larynx}

= Cricothyroid muscle
{parent=Laryngeal muscle}

= Vocal fold
{parent=Larynx}

= Glottis
{parent=Larynx}

= Gland
{parent=Anatomy}

= Thyroid
{parent=Gland}

= Goitre
{parent=Thyroid}

= Bulbourethral gland
{parent=Gland}

= Cowper's glands
{c}
{synonym}

= Cowper's gland
{c}
{synonym}

A paired male perineal gland beside the membranous <urethra>, deep to the <perineal membrane>. Its duct reaches the bulbar <urethra>.

= Salivary gland
{parent=Gland}

= Parotid gland
{parent=Salivary gland}

= Sublingual gland
{parent=Salivary gland}

= Submandibular gland
{parent=Salivary gland}

= Salivary secretion
{parent=Salivary gland}

= Oesophagus
{parent=Anatomy}

= Trachea
{parent=Anatomy}

